id: signature-technique
name: Signature Technique
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: true
requiresTarget: true
signatureTechnique: true
usageLimit: 1/round
tags: signature
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Throw one of your own Signature Techniques. One Action and once a Combat Round,
  whichever you pick, and the Technique's own KP Cost is what you pay.
text: >
  Signature Technique Maneuver [1/Round]: Blast an Opponent away with a Signature
  Technique!
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: Varies (each Signature Technique will have their own KP Cost – that is
  the KP Cost you pay for this Maneuver)
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Make an Attacking Maneuver using a Signature Technique you have access
  to.

---

# No script. What this Maneuver does is use a different Maneuver, and a script has
# no way to ask a player which - so `signatureTechnique: true` hands it to the code
# that can, the same way `charge` and `movement` are handled.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - you are asked which Signature Technique you have access to, before anything
#     is paid, so backing out of the question costs nothing
#   - the Action Cost is this Maneuver's: 1 Action, whatever the Technique's own
#     header says. A Technique is not a Maneuver you use, it is what you use this
#     one with
#   - the KP Cost is the Technique's - "that is the KP Cost you pay for this
#     Maneuver" - and so is the Profile, the target, the script and the card
#   - the use is recorded against this Maneuver, which is what makes [1/Round] a
#     limit across all of your Techniques rather than one apiece
#
# `tags: signature` is on this file rather than only on the Techniques, because
# this Maneuver is the only way to use one: a rule that forbids Signature
# Techniques - Transfigured does - has to stop this, and it reads the tag.
#
# --- What is not built, and why -----------------------------------------------
#
# Buying a Signature Technique with Technique Points. The rules for what a Technique
# costs to design and what its Advantages and Disadvantages are worth are not in
# this system yet, so there is nothing to spend TP against and no list to spend it
# from. A Technique is a Maneuver Item you build on the sheet and mark as one, and
# what it costs you at character creation is the table's to agree until that exists.
#
# The Advantages and Disadvantages themselves are half here: the files are under
# traits/signature/, `advantageWoundParts` does the arithmetic, and a Maneuver can
# now carry a list of them - what is missing is the part that prices them.
